1
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:11,370
(How to make enchanted knife.)
Some matters you have to solve it yourself.

2
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:11,920
Some matters you have to solve it yourself.

3
00:00:13,325 --> 00:00:14,840
Can't rely on anyone.

4
00:00:17,575 --> 00:00:20,372
No matter how far we run. He will find us.

5
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:23,400
That Gott. He's like bad karma.

6
00:00:24,142 --> 00:00:25,520
Following us everywhere.

7
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:28,733
But the karma itself...

8
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:31,440
it happens to involve the Satra Sutra book.

9
00:00:52,973 --> 00:00:54,619
Trust me, and you'll survive.

10
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:57,659
Bring me betel leaves and uncooked rice.

11
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:03,760
You bastard, Anon!

12
00:01:03,937 --> 00:01:04,760
You animal!

13
00:01:05,892 --> 00:01:06,709
You animal!

14
00:01:09,480 --> 00:01:10,240
You bastard!

15
00:02:03,474 --> 00:02:04,386
Help!

16
00:02:04,897 --> 00:02:05,740
Come quickly!

17
00:02:06,062 --> 00:02:07,975
Hey! Anyone outside, come look quickly!

18
00:02:10,146 --> 00:02:11,871
- Hurry!
- Hey, sir!

19
00:02:15,259 --> 00:02:16,820
Sir! Sir!

20
00:03:59,968 --> 00:04:01,342
This town will be mine.

21
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:07,770
All mine.

22
00:04:45,760 --> 00:04:48,040
No more running. Better to just fight.

23
00:04:48,817 --> 00:04:49,600
Let's settle this.

24
00:04:50,760 --> 00:04:52,560
I'll have Mom stay with Auntie
in Lampoon for a while.

25
00:04:55,561 --> 00:04:56,800
But in all my life,

26
00:04:57,116 --> 00:05:00,400
I've never seen anyone practice
black magic with such power.

27
00:05:01,297 --> 00:05:03,718
There was one time
when he was hit with incense ash.

28
00:05:04,539 --> 00:05:05,640
Did you see his face?

29
00:05:06,299 --> 00:05:08,466
Gott's face changed.

30
00:05:09,116 --> 00:05:11,000
It was like someone else
was inside his body.

31
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:24,782
Or maybe it's not human.

32
00:05:26,998 --> 00:05:28,111
It's not human, man.

33
00:05:29,370 --> 00:05:30,640
Oh, Uncle.

34
00:05:40,740 --> 00:05:43,283
But it's a consciousness
that refuses to be reborn.

35
00:05:44,280 --> 00:05:45,760
It lingers, obsessed with revenge.

36
00:05:46,520 --> 00:05:48,194
Trapped by the karma
it creates in every life.

37
00:05:49,380 --> 00:05:51,245
The reason it can inhabit a human body...

38
00:05:51,895 --> 00:05:53,320
is because it steals other people's bodies.

39
00:05:53,885 --> 00:05:54,880
After a long time,

40
00:05:55,391 --> 00:05:57,318
it consumes them and makes it its own body.

41
00:05:58,146 --> 00:05:59,833
That's why they call it
a 'possessing spirit.'

42
00:06:00,956 --> 00:06:02,612
Oh, and what does it want, Uncle?

43
00:06:07,363 --> 00:06:10,120
It's vicious. That means it wants revenge.

44
00:06:11,158 --> 00:06:12,086
It wants immortality.

45
00:06:13,043 --> 00:06:14,726
Lingering until it becomes a demon.
That's what.

46
00:06:17,714 --> 00:06:20,360
And what does that have to do
with the human-skin Satra Sutra book?

47
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:25,551
This Satra Sutra book...

48
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:28,940
If it can open that book,

49
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:31,446
it won't just become immortal.

50
00:06:32,848 --> 00:06:35,040
It will also be able to
control the evil spirits

51
00:06:35,074 --> 00:06:36,473
that are contained within that book.

52
00:06:37,123 --> 00:06:38,440
I don't think that's good news at all.

53
00:06:40,622 --> 00:06:42,448
And will there be no one
who can subdue it, Uncle?

54
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:46,940
There is one.

55
00:06:50,940 --> 00:06:51,940
Or maybe it's you guys.

56
00:07:53,297 --> 00:07:55,133
Aren't you quite something? Huh?

57
00:07:56,869 --> 00:07:59,492
Killing people and living a normal life.

58
00:08:01,304 --> 00:08:02,940
Truly, purely evil.

59
00:08:07,480 --> 00:08:08,880
You're thick with defilements.

60
00:08:11,480 --> 00:08:12,365
Greed.

61
00:08:13,280 --> 00:08:14,146
Desire.

62
00:08:15,420 --> 00:08:16,093
Stupidity.

63
00:08:20,966 --> 00:08:22,518
What's the plan now, you wicked man?

64
00:08:25,300 --> 00:08:27,533
- I will run for MP.
- Hmm.

65
00:08:28,834 --> 00:08:30,323
And I will become an MP.

66
00:08:30,939 --> 00:08:31,520
Hmm.

67
00:08:32,368 --> 00:08:34,285
Don't forget, here, money can buy anything.

68
00:08:36,208 --> 00:08:37,137
I told you.

69
00:08:38,299 --> 00:08:39,408
Sometimes,

70
00:08:40,608 --> 00:08:43,328
all those spells, charms, magical powers...

71
00:08:43,805 --> 00:08:45,377
might not even be a match for money.

72
00:08:46,041 --> 00:08:47,791
People here worship money as their god.

73
00:08:49,436 --> 00:08:50,313
It can buy anything.

74
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:52,768
And honestly,

75
00:08:53,871 --> 00:08:55,586
I don't have to work for anyone anymore.

76
00:08:56,713 --> 00:08:57,429
Hmm.

77
00:08:57,993 --> 00:08:59,196
This is humanity, huh.

78
00:09:00,726 --> 00:09:01,513
Yes.

79
00:09:02,546 --> 00:09:04,184
Unfearing of sin.

80
00:09:06,246 --> 00:09:08,619
No reverence, no faith.

81
00:09:10,483 --> 00:09:13,377
How many times do I have to
show you people?

82
00:09:17,885 --> 00:09:19,500
You don't chant praises.

83
00:09:22,820 --> 00:09:27,304
You question those you should revere.
Hard-hearted.

84
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:30,695
Where have the prayers gone?
Where are they?

85
00:09:32,462 --> 00:09:34,285
Your life...

86
00:09:34,900 --> 00:09:38,040
Is your suffering too little that
you dare declare war on me? Huh?

87
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:51,160
A man like you...

88
00:09:53,400 --> 00:09:55,840
must serve me for the rest of your life.

89
00:09:58,462 --> 00:09:59,280
That's it.

90
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:01,220
Thelo Moggallano.

91
00:11:01,846 --> 00:11:03,617
Antaradhayitva.

92
00:11:04,083 --> 00:11:06,747
Bhūmisukhumam Pramano.

93
00:11:07,172 --> 00:11:09,620
Bhagavato Iddhiya.

94
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:12,278
Attano Sarire.

95
00:11:12,636 --> 00:11:13,638
Mamsam.

96
00:11:14,003 --> 00:11:15,210
Lohitam.

97
00:11:30,880 --> 00:11:31,920
From now on,

98
00:11:32,528 --> 00:11:35,240
you are the one with the Wind element
as your spiritual power.

99
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:03,843
And you...

100
00:12:05,680 --> 00:12:07,227
are the one with the Water element

101
00:12:07,666 --> 00:12:08,504
as your spiritual power.

102
00:13:27,756 --> 00:13:30,140
The Burmese soldiers' corpses
were beheaded for ritual sacrifice.

103
00:13:34,226 --> 00:13:35,474
There are no bodies of our men.

104
00:13:39,780 --> 00:13:41,408
The soldiers' sword tips have no blood.

105
00:13:45,560 --> 00:13:46,643
They have protective charms.

106
00:13:50,490 --> 00:13:51,960
Those ghost army bastards.

107
00:13:54,772 --> 00:13:56,260
The rumors are true.

108
00:13:57,050 --> 00:13:57,965
That they...

109
00:13:58,680 --> 00:14:01,560
have a ghost army protecting Bang Rajan.

110
00:14:02,570 --> 00:14:03,800
If they use ghosts for protection,

111
00:14:06,640 --> 00:14:08,316
we will use ghosts to kill them.

112
00:14:25,979 --> 00:14:27,408
To a good rebirth, my friend.

113
00:14:36,768 --> 00:14:38,594
I think we should hurry and
ell the people at Bang Rajan.

114
00:14:39,099 --> 00:14:40,963
The Burmese know we're here now.

115
00:14:42,059 --> 00:14:42,643
Mm-hmm.

116
00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:46,177
I think we should have Thong...

117
00:14:47,620 --> 00:14:48,695
go tell the Ban Rajan villagers.

118
00:14:49,732 --> 00:14:50,890
He knows the routes well.

119
00:15:23,280 --> 00:15:24,800
It's a trap.

120
00:17:05,144 --> 00:17:06,949
You can't fight it.

121
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:09,502
I have to help my nephew.

122
00:17:10,038 --> 00:17:11,530
As I promised to Itt.

123
00:17:12,577 --> 00:17:14,020
It's karma.

124
00:17:14,240 --> 00:17:17,000
Each person's karma from their past lives.

125
00:17:18,166 --> 00:17:20,020
And there's really no way
to resolve karma, Uncle?

126
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:24,540
Karma, no matter how many lifetimes...

127
00:17:24,970 --> 00:17:26,038
it never ends.

128
00:17:27,116 --> 00:17:30,280
If the creditors of your karma
don't forgive you.

129
00:17:31,415 --> 00:17:34,800
And you keep creating enmity and karma
with each other in every life...

130
00:17:36,469 --> 00:17:38,840
You have to stop one of them.

131
00:17:39,443 --> 00:17:41,240
To stop the karma in this lifetime.

132
00:17:52,480 --> 00:17:55,283
You idiot! You should have raised your bet!
You dumbass!

133
00:17:55,537 --> 00:17:56,120
There!

134
00:17:56,320 --> 00:17:56,960
Right there!

135
00:17:57,240 --> 00:17:58,240
Go! Go!

136
00:17:59,200 --> 00:18:00,852
Whoa, hey!

137
00:18:01,332 --> 00:18:03,078
Play properly! You'll do it!

138
00:18:05,130 --> 00:18:07,777
Whoa! Damn it!

139
00:18:09,400 --> 00:18:10,156
Damn!

140
00:18:35,676 --> 00:18:38,010
I'll have Mom stay at Uncle Pong's house
in Lampoon for a while, Uncle.

141
00:18:39,280 --> 00:18:40,114
As for the shop,

142
00:18:40,760 --> 00:18:41,718
it's up to them.

143
00:18:44,024 --> 00:18:45,339
I see they're happy.

144
00:18:45,812 --> 00:18:47,645
I don't want to destroy their dreams.

145
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:50,900
And what about your life?

146
00:18:51,485 --> 00:18:52,222
What are you going to do?

147
00:18:53,356 --> 00:18:54,709
Your life is your own.

148
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:56,977
You're always taking care of others.

149
00:18:57,320 --> 00:18:58,556
Don't you take care of yourself at all?

150
00:19:11,640 --> 00:19:12,365
Singh.

151
00:19:15,189 --> 00:19:16,473
I have nothing to give you.

152
00:19:18,052 --> 00:19:19,220
Except this arcane knife.

153
00:19:19,353 --> 00:19:20,700
That your father gave me.

154
00:19:22,493 --> 00:19:23,610
Take it for self-defense.

155
00:19:27,880 --> 00:19:29,760
You'll need it more than I will.

156
00:19:33,560 --> 00:19:34,680
And remember, Singh...

157
00:19:36,309 --> 00:19:37,880
If it tries to lure you in,

158
00:19:38,841 --> 00:19:40,800
don't ever fall into dark arts.

159
00:19:47,373 --> 00:19:48,160
Thanks, Uncle.

160
00:20:08,600 --> 00:20:09,640
You're up to this, kid?

161
00:20:14,280 --> 00:20:14,960
I am.

162
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:18,240
I was never afraid of anything.

163
00:20:21,353 --> 00:20:23,200
And you're not afraid of Gott or Anon?

164
00:20:27,290 --> 00:20:28,640
If they have the guts, let them come.

165
00:20:29,880 --> 00:20:31,120
We've never been afraid to die anyway.

166
00:20:36,560 --> 00:20:38,000
And aren't you afraid that...

167
00:20:39,280 --> 00:20:40,480
something will happen to Singh?

168
00:20:46,010 --> 00:20:46,539
Hey!

169
00:20:47,360 --> 00:20:47,960
- What are you talking about?
- Fucker!

170
00:20:48,093 --> 00:20:48,803
What were you talking about?

171
00:20:49,680 --> 00:20:53,240
- You spooked me just now.
- You see me all day and still get scared?

172
00:20:53,516 --> 00:20:55,944
I asked her if she wasn't
worried about Singh.

173
00:20:56,200 --> 00:20:57,600
You're really nosy.

174
00:20:58,198 --> 00:20:59,640
So, aren't you worried?

175
00:21:02,560 --> 00:21:03,040
Hmm.

176
00:21:07,380 --> 00:21:08,380
Of course I'm worried.

177
00:21:12,320 --> 00:21:12,760
Ah-ha!

178
00:21:13,360 --> 00:21:13,800
Ah-ha!

179
00:21:13,880 --> 00:21:15,800
Ah-ha-ha-ha-ha!

180
00:21:16,920 --> 00:21:18,280
There's a reaction! There's a reaction!

181
00:21:18,840 --> 00:21:20,600
Face red, cheeks red like this.

182
00:21:21,720 --> 00:21:22,640
Don't tell me...

183
00:21:23,200 --> 00:21:24,280
our tiger...

184
00:21:24,400 --> 00:21:26,960
has already managed to
devour the little deer's heart.

185
00:21:27,720 --> 00:21:28,600
That must be it!

186
00:21:29,043 --> 00:21:29,822
What are you saying?

187
00:21:30,302 --> 00:21:31,080
I don't know.

188
00:21:31,314 --> 00:21:33,040
I had this experience back in junior high.

189
00:21:33,600 --> 00:21:37,040
I know, I can tell.
I knew it, that damn prick.

190
00:21:37,440 --> 00:21:39,440
The tiger stayed quiet around me.

191
00:21:40,040 --> 00:21:42,080
You guys snuck off and
did it already, no wonder!

192
00:21:42,400 --> 00:21:44,760
I invited him to watch porn and
he didn't want to hang out with me.

193
00:21:45,088 --> 00:21:45,600
Hmph.

194
00:21:45,680 --> 00:21:46,680
- Huh?
- Distant.

195
00:21:48,360 --> 00:21:50,760
Hey, no need to be shy.
It's a common, everyone goes through it.

196
00:21:51,320 --> 00:21:52,120
It's normal.

197
00:21:52,413 --> 00:21:53,160
Come on.

198
00:21:53,640 --> 00:21:54,800
I've been with Singh since you were kids.

199
00:21:55,560 --> 00:21:56,200
Well.

200
00:22:38,720 --> 00:22:39,360
Damn.

201
00:23:22,295 --> 00:23:24,486
Didn't I tell you not to follow me?

202
00:23:26,360 --> 00:23:27,800
I just wanted to talk to you.

203
00:23:30,497 --> 00:23:31,920
You're really stubborn, huh.

204
00:23:37,040 --> 00:23:38,240
I just want to ask you...

205
00:23:41,440 --> 00:23:42,600
to stop interfering with me.

206
00:23:47,160 --> 00:23:48,240
I want to become an MP.

207
00:23:50,160 --> 00:23:51,400
And make money in this business.

208
00:23:53,471 --> 00:23:54,702
Which I can do without you.

209
00:23:58,111 --> 00:23:59,401
However much money you want, just tell me.

210
00:23:59,680 --> 00:24:00,608
I only ask for one thing.

211
00:24:03,800 --> 00:24:04,646
Stop interfering with me.

212
00:24:04,880 --> 00:24:05,240
Okay?

213
00:24:14,200 --> 00:24:15,000
You...

214
00:24:15,360 --> 00:24:17,160
are you negotiating with me?

215
00:24:18,876 --> 00:24:19,560
No.

216
00:24:22,434 --> 00:24:23,429
I'm not negotiating.

217
00:24:36,680 --> 00:24:37,840
Backstabbing dog.

218
00:24:39,920 --> 00:24:41,015
You're such a bastard.

219
00:24:44,360 --> 00:24:45,360
A person like you...

220
00:24:47,320 --> 00:24:48,520
just clutters up the world.

221
00:25:08,160 --> 00:25:08,560
I...

222
00:25:09,040 --> 00:25:10,840
I know where the person
you want to find is.

223
00:25:30,640 --> 00:25:31,377
Tell me.

224
00:25:34,354 --> 00:25:35,276
I said...

225
00:25:36,306 --> 00:25:37,725
I found the person you're looking for.

226
00:25:38,994 --> 00:25:39,780
I found her.

227
00:25:45,293 --> 00:25:47,005
Hey, bro, I'll owe you for now, okay?

228
00:25:47,840 --> 00:25:49,986
I have money for you. I won't stiff you.

229
00:25:51,200 --> 00:25:53,080
Really, bro... I never stiff people.

230
00:25:53,120 --> 00:25:55,040
Hey, bro, don't you remember?
I just paid you back.

231
00:25:55,160 --> 00:25:56,420
It isn't that long ago!

232
00:25:57,714 --> 00:25:58,208
<i>Hey!</i>

233
00:25:58,360 --> 00:26:00,780
<i>But last night you owe me
two hundred thousand in one go.</i>

234
00:26:00,880 --> 00:26:02,274
<i>That's not including the old debt.</i>

235
00:26:02,650 --> 00:26:03,182
Whoa, bro!

236
00:26:03,363 --> 00:26:05,140
Who knew he'd miss so badly?

237
00:26:05,320 --> 00:26:07,560
He's been playing well
the whole season, bro!

238
00:26:08,813 --> 00:26:09,857
<i>When will you transfer it to me?</i>

239
00:26:12,560 --> 00:26:13,040
Uh...

240
00:26:13,401 --> 00:26:14,622
How about mid-month, bro?

241
00:26:14,900 --> 00:26:16,680
And bro, remember what I told you?

242
00:26:16,932 --> 00:26:18,080
About meeting the shaman?

243
00:26:18,320 --> 00:26:19,200
In prison, yeah?

244
00:26:19,880 --> 00:26:20,990
He gave me fucking winning numbers.

245
00:26:21,020 --> 00:26:23,600
This round I'll win, bro!
I'll pay you back immediately.

246
00:26:24,257 --> 00:26:25,756
Hey, but don't tell anyone, bro!

247
00:26:26,932 --> 00:26:28,080
Okay? I'm counting on you, bro.

248
00:26:28,680 --> 00:26:29,360
You...

249
00:26:29,560 --> 00:26:30,960
Just get me the money.

250
00:26:31,787 --> 00:26:33,606
<i>If not, I won't let you go.</i>

251
00:26:34,681 --> 00:26:36,786
<i>I'll send people to beat you up every day.</i>

252
00:26:37,168 --> 00:26:38,600
<i>Until you get the money for me.</i>

253
00:26:46,840 --> 00:26:48,800
Manchester United.
Manchester United? You shithead!

254
00:27:22,862 --> 00:27:23,645
What are the numbers for this draw?

255
00:27:31,320 --> 00:27:31,892
Hey!

256
00:27:32,194 --> 00:27:33,206
What's the winning number this month?

257
00:27:33,880 --> 00:27:35,040
Hurry up and tell me!

258
00:27:35,885 --> 00:27:37,704
So I can go bet quickly
before they stop selling.

259
00:27:38,935 --> 00:27:41,100
And next time you want anything, tell me.
I'll get it for you.

260
00:27:43,293 --> 00:27:45,137
0 4 6.

261
00:27:46,306 --> 00:27:46,720
Huh?

262
00:27:48,594 --> 00:27:50,236
064? 046? What?

263
00:27:52,240 --> 00:27:52,890
What?

264
00:27:59,000 --> 00:28:00,600
He could have told me clearly.

265
00:29:05,720 --> 00:29:06,720
Damn it.

266
00:29:08,125 --> 00:29:08,760
You bastard.

267
00:29:12,027 --> 00:29:13,081
No budget for a funeral.

268
00:29:13,593 --> 00:29:14,918
And just bury him like this?

269
00:29:16,840 --> 00:29:17,982
Pathetic as hell.

270
00:29:18,520 --> 00:29:19,168
Ugh!

271
00:29:21,160 --> 00:29:21,704
Go.

272
00:29:23,206 --> 00:29:23,822
Come.

273
00:29:26,445 --> 00:29:27,853
Hey, you bastard!

274
